  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, describes Project Orion, a US plan in the 1950s and 60s to push spacecraft using nuclear power. He says Air Force general Curtis LeMay wanted it and the physicist Freeman Dyson worked on it, but President John F. Kennedy was strongly against it, so it was dropped. He tells it as an example of bold space ideas that were stopped."
